drm: h713-afbd: the expected handoff state is a board fact, and the refusal names it

h713_afbd_probe() reads three register words the boot loader leaves behind
and refuses with -ENODEV unless they are three literals: AFBD_CTRL 0x03001901
(the RGB channel live with its commit armed), AFBD_VIDEO_CTRL 0x03000010
(source 0 idle - the active word is H713_VIDEO_CTRL_ACTIVE 0x03000013), and
the LVDS selector at lvds + 0x06c 0x29000000 (RGB selected downstream - the
video variant is H713_VIDEO_SELECTOR 0x39000000). The driver restores exactly
these three words when the video plane goes away again
(h713_afbd_video_disable()), which is why it insists on them: it is the state
it can put back.

The refusal is right and stays. The three numbers, though, are a bench
measurement on one board compiled into a driver that is otherwise carefully
board-independent - it reads its geometry, its stride and its source address
out of the hardware twenty lines earlier (analysis A11, 18.09.2026,
umbau/reviews/A11.md section 6: "the one hardcoded board fact left in this
driver"). A board with a different panel port count or a different firmware
generation fails the check, and its owner has no way to describe his board
and no way to see what was wrong.

So two things change, and nothing else:

(a) The refusal prints all six words - what was read and what was expected,
    one pair per register - and says when the node carried no expectation of
    its own. A foreign owner's log then states the fact instead of a verdict.

(b) The expected triple comes from an optional device-tree property on the
    afbd node, allwinner,handoff-state = <ctrl video_ctrl selector>. Absent,
    the driver uses today's literals, now named and commented next to the
    constants they belong with. The property is documented in the display
    node's comment in sun50i-h713.dtsi; this node has no binding file in the
    tree, so there is no binding text to follow.

Tested on the HY310: byte-identical behaviour. Its device tree does not carry
the property (of_property_read_u32_array returns -EINVAL, the defaults stay),
the three comparisons are the same three comparisons, and the only reachable
difference is the wording of a message that is not printed on a board that
passes. The dtsi hunk is a comment; the compiled DTB is unchanged.

diff -ruN a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
@@ -141,6 +141,24 @@
 #define H713_VIDEO_CTRL_FORMAT	GENMASK(14, 8)
 #define H713_VIDEO_SELECTOR	0x39000000
 
+/*
+ * The handoff this driver takes over from: AFBD_CTRL with the RGB channel
+ * live and its commit armed, AFBD_VIDEO_CTRL with source 0 idle (the active
+ * word is H713_VIDEO_CTRL_ACTIVE), and the downstream selector pointing at
+ * RGB (the video variant is H713_VIDEO_SELECTOR). The three words were
+ * measured on the HY310 and are the default. A board whose boot loader or
+ * panel port count leaves different words says its own in
+ * "allwinner,handoff-state" -- <ctrl video_ctrl selector> -- because this is
+ * a fact about the board, not about the chip, and a foreign board must be
+ * able to describe it instead of failing a check it cannot influence.
+ */
+#define H713_HANDOFF_WORDS	3
+static const u32 h713_afbd_handoff_default[H713_HANDOFF_WORDS] = {
+	0x03001901,	/* AFBD_CTRL     -- RGB channel active */
+	0x03000010,	/* AFBD_VIDEO_CTRL -- source 0 idle */
+	0x29000000,	/* LVDS + 0x06c  -- RGB selected downstream */
+};
+
 /* The AFBD consumes the picture in 16x16 blocks. */
 #define H713_VIDEO_BLOCK	16u
 
@@ -1774,6 +1792,7 @@
 	struct h713_afbd *h;
 	struct drm_device *drm;
 	struct resource res;
+	u32 want[H713_HANDOFF_WORDS];
 	unsigned long flags;
 	int irq, ret;
 
@@ -1912,11 +1931,22 @@
 	 */
 	h->video_c_stride_idle = readl(h->regs + AFBD_VIDEO_C_STRIDE);
 	h->selector_rgb = readl(h->lvds_regs + 0x06c);
-	if (h->video_ctrl_idle != 0x03000010 ||
-	    h->rgb_ctrl_active != 0x03001901 ||
-	    h->selector_rgb != 0x29000000)
+
+	memcpy(want, h713_afbd_handoff_default, sizeof(want));
+	ret = of_property_read_u32_array(dev->of_node, "allwinner,handoff-state",
+					 want, H713_HANDOFF_WORDS);
+	if (ret && ret != -EINVAL)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
+				     "bad allwinner,handoff-state\n");
+	if (h->rgb_ctrl_active != want[0] ||
+	    h->video_ctrl_idle != want[1] ||
+	    h->selector_rgb != want[2])
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, -ENODEV,
-			"video handoff state is not the validated register configuration\n");
+			"video handoff state is not this board's: CTRL %08x (expected %08x), VIDEO_CTRL %08x (expected %08x), selector %08x (expected %08x)%s\n",
+			h->rgb_ctrl_active, want[0],
+			h->video_ctrl_idle, want[1],
+			h->selector_rgb, want[2],
+			ret ? " -- the node has no allwinner,handoff-state" : "");
 
 	ret = drmm_mode_config_init(drm);
 	if (ret)
diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -1872,6 +1872,20 @@
 			 */
 			memory-region = <&mips_framebuf>, <&viddec_info>;
 			memory-region-names = "hdmi-ring", "viddec-info";
+			/*
+			 * Optional: allwinner,handoff-state = <ctrl
+			 * video_ctrl selector>, the three register words the
+			 * boot loader must have left behind before this
+			 * driver takes over - AFBD_CTRL (0x140) with the RGB
+			 * channel live, AFBD_VIDEO_CTRL (0x010) with source 0
+			 * idle, and the LVDS selector (lvds + 0x06c) pointing
+			 * at RGB. Left out here, so the driver uses the words
+			 * measured on the HY310: 0x03001901, 0x03000010,
+			 * 0x29000000. A board whose boot loader or panel port
+			 * count hands over other words puts them in its own
+			 * board file; the driver still refuses to probe on a
+			 * mismatch, and names all six words when it does.
+			 */
 			status = "okay";
 		};
 
